{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_459","type":"reasoning","text":"Everything is in place. Let me do one last check: verify the reverify spec is valid with the harness validate --no-diff, and the guard file's ASCII `\\u2264` escape renders correctly. Actually I used literal `\\u2264` inside a JSON patch — applied_patch wrote the literal characters `\\u2264` into the TS file inside a string literal, which TypeScript will interpret as the ≤ character at runtime. Let me verify.\n\nActually in the file content I saw `expect(spec).toContain(\"p99 \\u2264 80ms\");` — the `\\u2264` inside a double-quoted TS string is a valid escape for ≤. Good.\n\nAnd `expect(spec).toMatch(/\\u2265\\s*0\\.90/);` — this is a regex literal `/\\u2265\\s*0\\.90/` which matches ≥ followed by optional whitespace and \"0.90\". The spec has `≥ 0.90` so there's a space. Actually the spec text is \"≥ 0.90\" but wait — in the spec it's \"≥ 90%\" and \"≥ 0.90\"? Let me check. The spec body says: `**Deferral agreement rate** ≥ 90%: \\`deferralAgreementCount / (agreement + disagreement) ≥ 0.90\\` over 10 waves.` So \"≥ 0.90\" exists. Good, the regex matches.\n\nMy earlier node probe confirmed the regex matched: \"agreement >= 0.90 regex PASS\". Good.\n\nEverything checks out. Let me write the final summary."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_460","type":"agent_message","text":"All deliverables are in place and verified. Here's the summary.\n\n**Outcome**\n\nA02 re-verified the A2 multi-agent orchestration controlled pilot gate against the **original** spec thresholds (no redefinition). The honest verdict is **NO-GO**, not pass.\n\n- **Criteria 1-3 PASS** — mapped to current executable evidence at unchanged thresholds: (1) `checkBudgetViolation('a2')` → `degrade_to_live_only` when deferral disagreement > 10%, (2) `ResourceAwareWaveScheduler` rejects re-plan of a started wave (`wave_started`), (3) p99 ≤ 80ms partition.\n- **Criterion 4 NO-GO residual** — multi-worker resume creating new sessions (criterion 3.7) has *no dedicated test* in the current tree; recorded as a residual, not claimed as passing.\n\n**Spec drift fixed** in `harness/specs/tasks/a2-multi-agent-orchestration-pilot.md`\n- Removed two references to paths that don't exist in the tree: `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts` and `openclaw_runtime/src/agents/cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts` (the `cross-area/` directory is absent).\n- Wired the counter tests that cover criteria 1/5 into `requiredTests`; threshold text byte-unchanged.\n\n**Files created**\n- `tests/unit/a02-a2-gate-coverage.test.ts` — guard driving the real runtime modules (criteria 1/2/5) and pinning the spec wiring + drift removal.\n- `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a02-orchestration-pilot-reverify.md`\n- `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a02-a2-orchestration-gate.md`, `a02-acceptance.json` (`decision.status: NO-GO`), `A02-SHA256SUMS`\n- `.rsi/RESULT.json`\n\n**Checks actually run** (offline, all exit 0): harness `validate` on both specs, spec lifecycle, evidence-refs, no-BOM, policy-docs, B00 baseline structure, credential scan (0 hits), `sha256sum -c A02-SHA256SUMS` (5/5), and a Node type-strip replay of the guard assertions against the real modules (`a2` 8/3 → `degrade_to_live_only`; 10/1 → not violated; started-wave rePlan →